-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 70: define the `note_about` edge table as a proper
--   TYPE RELATION FROM note TO source
-- so the note↔source auto-link feature (Track NS) can persist "this note is
-- about this source" links — found by embedding cosine — as real graph edges
-- that can be RELATEd, traversed, drawn and exported, alongside the note↔note
-- `related_note` edges (migration 68) and source↔source `source_verdict` edges
-- (migration 69).
--
-- Background. Track NS (note→source auto-link) extends Track Y: a note links to
-- the SOURCES it most resembles (cosine of `note.embedding` vs the source
-- aggregate `source.embedding` — same mxbai-embed-large 1024-dim space) and
-- stores each link as a `note_about` edge. The table is BRAND NEW — no prior
-- migration defines it — so on any DB (fresh container or staging) it would
-- otherwise be auto-created by the first RELATE as the SurrealDB default
--   DEFINE TABLE note_about TYPE ANY SCHEMALESS
-- which stores an untyped record, NOT a graph edge. This is the exact drift
-- class the `mentions`/`cites`/`related_note`/`source_verdict` migrations
-- (66/67/68/69) fixed; 70 defines it correctly up front so the auto-link writer
-- always lands a typed `note -> note_about -> source` edge.
--
-- Naming / ontology. `note_about` mirrors the lowercase, snake_case,
-- type-prefixed edge-naming convention of `related_note` (68) and
-- `source_verdict` (69), and echoes schema.org/about ("this note is about this
-- source"). It does NOT collide with the ontology's uppercase `ABOUT`
-- relationship type (schema_core.yaml), which is an entity↔entity KG relation —
-- a different layer from this note↔document edge.
--
-- Strategy (mirrors migrations 66/67/68/69's non-destructive remediation):
--   1. DELETE only null-endpoint junk rows (in = NONE OR out = NONE). A real
--      `note_about` edge always has non-null in/out, so this is a no-op on a
--      healthy table and only clears the non-edge junk a drifted/auto-created
--      TYPE ANY table could hold (which would otherwise block the RELATION
--      redefine). A blanket `DELETE note_about` would WIPE healthy edges — the
--      destructive mistake migration 58 made; 62/66/67/68/69 fixed it with this
--      null-endpoint-only predicate and 70 follows suit.
--   2. DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE ... TYPE RELATION FROM note TO source. On
--      SurrealDB v2 OVERWRITE converts a drifted/auto-created TYPE ANY table to
--      RELATION; on an already-correct RELATION table it re-asserts the
--      identical definition and PRESERVES existing edge records (the
--      migration-62/66/67/68/69 empirical fact, re-checked for `note_about` by
--      this track's container tests). `note_about` is a regenerated projection
--      (auto-link clears and re-relates per note), so there is no canonical edge
--      state worth a destructive rollback.
--   3. DEFINE the edge fields with OVERWRITE. `similarity_score` is the cosine
--      that drove the link (the per-edge "why", for thresholding the viz /
--      triage, parallel to `related_note.similarity_score`). `method` records
--      how the link was derived (`"embedding"` today). `created_at` mirrors
--      66/67/68/69 for provenance parity.
--
-- Strict-field / S.4 note. Every strict field below carries a DEFAULT, and the
-- table is EMPTY on every existing DB (it is brand new — 0 rows everywhere), so
-- there are NO pre-existing rows to drift and NO backfill UPDATE is required
-- (the S.4 hazard is a strict field with no default added to a table that
-- already holds rows; neither condition applies here). The auto-link writer
-- supplies `similarity_score`/`method` explicitly via RELATE-with-SET, so the
-- DEFAULTs are a safety floor, never the live value.
--
-- Idempotent + forward-only: the DELETE matches nothing on a second pass and
-- every OVERWRITE re-asserts an identical definition. Down is a documented
-- no-op (a schema definition has no faithful inverse; reverting to TYPE ANY
-- would re-break `RELATE note -> note_about -> source` — the very correctness
-- this establishes — and the edge set is a regenerated projection).
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. Drop ONLY null-endpoint junk rows (the non-edge records a drifted/
--    auto-created TYPE ANY table could hold). Real `note_about` edges always
--    have non-null in/out, so this never touches them — no-op on a fresh empty
--    table AND on any healthy edge set.
DELETE note_about WHERE in = NONE OR out = NONE;

-- 2. Assert the canonical edge definition. Converts a drifted/auto-created
--    TYPE ANY table to RELATION note->source on v2; identical no-op (edges
--    preserved) on an already-correct RELATION table.
DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE note_about SCHEMAFULL TYPE RELATION FROM note TO source;

-- 3. Edge fields (all strict WITH defaults — S.4 safe). `similarity_score` is
--    the cosine similarity that drove the link; `method` is how it was derived
--    (`"embedding"` today); `created_at` is provenance (mirrors 66/67/68/69).
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE similarity_score ON note_about TYPE float DEFAULT 0.0;
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE method ON note_about TYPE string DEFAULT "embedding";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE created_at ON note_about TYPE datetime DEFAULT time::now();

-- Index on similarity_score so the auto-link triage / viz can threshold edges
-- (mirrors idx_related_note_score / idx_cites_confidence). OVERWRITE so a
-- re-apply converges.
DEFINE INDEX OVERWRITE idx_note_about_score ON note_about FIELDS similarity_score;
